{
  "id": "vidsmallerPreflight",
  "name": "Pre-flight check video URLs against Discord, WhatsApp and Gmail upload limits",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "79bf8c34-423e-4bce-9ddf-96ac1da32781",
      "name": "Sticky Note 0",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1180,
        -1160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 560,
        "content": "# Video upload pre-flight check\n\n**Stop discovering upload limits at the upload dialog.** Give this workflow a list of video URLs and it tells you, per platform, which ones will upload and what the rest have to be compressed to - without downloading a single file.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. A `HEAD` request reads each video's size from its `Content-Length` header. A few hundred bytes per video, not hundreds of megabytes.\n2. [VidSmaller](https://vidsmaller.com)'s free API turns that size into a verdict: the platform's real limit, whether the file clears it, and the settings that would make it fit.\n3. Results are split three ways - ready / too big / size unknown - merged, and reported.\n\n### Why not just hardcode the limits\n\nBecause they move and they lie. Discord raised its free cap from 10 MB to 20 MB in August 2026 and its own FAQ still said 10 MB weeks later. Gmail's \"25 MB\" is really ~18 MB of file, because the attachment is measured *after* base64 encoding. Telegram's 2 GB does not apply to bots, which stop at 50 MB.\n\nThe API returns every limit with a `verifiedAt` date and a link to the platform's own documentation, plus a `safeTargetMb` that sits below the stated cap - because a target-size encode lands within a couple of percent, and two percent *over* a hard ceiling is a failed upload.\n\n### Setup\n\n**None.** No API key, no account, no credentials. Click **Execute workflow** and it runs on four real, public sample videos across three platforms.\n\nDocs: [vidsmaller.com/api-docs](https://vidsmaller.com/api-docs) \u00b7 Rate limit: 600 requests/hour/IP."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4e9a5ba8-ea13-45ba-a438-cfcfe69fdba4",
      "name": "Sticky Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1180,
        -520
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## 1 \u00b7 Two ways in\n\n**Execute workflow** runs the four samples below.\n\nThe **Webhook** is the production entry point. POST it a list and it answers with the report:\n\n```\ncurl -X POST <webhook-url> \\\n  -H \"content-type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"videos\": [\n      {\n        \"label\": \"clip\",\n        \"url\": \"https://example.com/clip.mp4\",\n        \"platform\": \"discord\",\n        \"durationSeconds\": 45\n      }\n    ]\n  }'\n```\n\n`platform` accepts `discord`, `whatsapp`, `email`, `telegram`, `slack`, `instagram`, `tiktok`, `twitter`. `durationSeconds` is optional but worth sending - without it nothing can judge whether the target size is comfortable or brutal."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "6d06b174-5f39-4a64-833c-a96354ad6f6e",
      "name": "Sticky Note 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -520,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 580,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "## 2 \u00b7 Measure, without downloading\n\n`HEAD` asks the server for the headers it would send for a `GET`, then stops. The file itself is never transferred.\n\nBoth nodes are deliberately forgiving: a 404, a dead host or a missing `Content-Length` header marks that one video as *size unknown* and the batch carries on."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4f4bcb62-6f3e-4806-84ab-21f5279755f2",
      "name": "Sticky Note 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        100,
        -280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## 3 \u00b7 Ask VidSmaller\n\nOne free, key-less call per video.\n\nIt returns the platform's stated limit, the safe target, the caveat that makes the stated limit misleading, a source list, the predicted output size, and `verdict` - which the next node switches on."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7d6a1f4d-0dd0-4a4c-bd58-4c5b1db0958c",
      "name": "Sticky Note 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        560,
        -280
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 420,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## 4 \u00b7 Act on the verdict\n\nThree shapes, one schema, so the report can treat them alike.\n\nSwap either branch for whatever you actually do: post to Slack, move the file, kick off a compression job, fail a CI check."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "14134687-c08b-4142-aecb-1dec9597898c",
      "name": "Sticky Note 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1020,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 580,
        "height": 180,
        "content": "## 5 \u00b7 Merge and report\n\nThe three branches are appended back into one list, counted, and turned into a plain-text report plus the raw rows.\n\n`Respond to Webhook` returns it to the caller. Replace it with Slack, Gmail, Sheets, or a database node for scheduled runs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
